{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 881 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "854e6a05371a2bb3eefb59ef1e01009f8db04f96eeef5e77f3bed99f13c560f6" :edb/db-before-t 880 :edb/db-after-t 881 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534193 50 #inst "2026-10-06T09:34:53.060Z" 13194139534193 true] [17592186115301 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281608 13194139534193 true] [17592186115302 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281601 13194139534193 true] [17592186115302 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281621 13194139534193 true] [17592186115794 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534193 true] [17592186115794 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981111/assets/8e7daf95fadbe2262a09e8183f00d63075655f3b97dd363984c192ac3414ad17.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" 13194139534193 true] [17592186115794 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/q-47650.png)\n\nConsider the function $y = f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" 13194139534193 false] [17592186115794 1145 "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-2$ the function has a cusp, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=2$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-2$, $x=0$, and $x=2.$" 13194139534193 true] [17592186115797 1017 #edb/ref 17592186114153 13194139534193 false] [17592186115797 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281615 13194139534193 true] [17592186115797 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534193 true] [17592186115797 1100 "Which of the following functions is differentiable at the point $x = 3$?" 13194139534193 false] [17592186115797 1100 "Which of the following functions is differentiable at the point $x=3?$" 13194139534193 true] [17592186115797 1145 "Notice that the function $p(x)$ is differentiable for all $x>0.$ Therefore, the correct answer is $p(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\nOther functions are not differentiable at $x=3.$\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=3$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ has a corner point at $x=3$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $h(x)$ has a vertical tangent at  $x=3$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $q(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=3$, so it is not differentiable there." 13194139534193 true] [17592186281601 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281602 13194139534193 true] [17592186281601 1089 "q-101991" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281601 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534193 true] [17592186281601 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981111/assets/6ec1bb6f164aa4878480f06707722769d1e17ff735a04c29a3fc2b9bd09ca467.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281601 1113 #uuid "8b49effd-34ee-539b-94bb-4a761d8bf290" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281601 1145 "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-10$ the function has a corner, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=-5$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-10$ and $x=-5.$" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281603 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281604 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281605 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281606 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281607 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1041 "selection" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281605 13194139534193 true] [17592186281602 1110 #uuid "d1a74be8-16fd-5929-85ad-92fc12e791c8" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281603 1034 "$x=-10$ only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281603 1111 #uuid "71541ac7-8988-5aa5-9dcf-893226b0bdd1" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281604 1034 "$x=-10,$ $x=-5,$  and $x=0$" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281604 1111 #uuid "343d1790-9290-574e-aea2-cddafbb5cf00" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281605 1034 "$x=-10$ and $x=-5$ only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281605 1111 #uuid "abea6dbd-cbc4-5e27-a20a-3c43e9c4070a" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281606 1034 "$x=-5$ only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281606 1111 #uuid "b5f653f3-165c-5e22-b98b-66497534353a" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281607 1034 "$x=0$ only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281607 1111 #uuid "ce7a9e75-e0dd-5c1a-a5a5-6d6160328651" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281608 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281609 13194139534193 true] [17592186281608 1089 "q-102163" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281608 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534193 true] [17592186281608 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x-2, & x<0 \\\\ -2, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\n- It is continuous at $x=0$\n- It is differentiable at $x=0$\n- It is differentiable on the interval $(0,2)$" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281608 1113 #uuid "c7c7ee1b-da55-5996-923f-38ff8f88ec23" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281608 1145 "- Statement I is true  Indeed, let's investigate the continuity of $f(x).$ It is continuous everywhere except, possibly, at  $x=0.$ At this point, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(2x-2)=2(0)-2=-2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}-2=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=f(0)=-2,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$ .\n\n- Statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=0$ because it has a corner point there: \n\n$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=2\\,$  if  $\\,x<0$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0\\,$ if $\\,x>0$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $f(x)$ is differentiable everywhere except at $x=0.$   Since $x=0$  doesn't belong to $(0,2)$, the given function is differentiable on this interval.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281610 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281611 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281612 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281613 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281614 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1041 "selection" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281611 13194139534193 true] [17592186281609 1110 #uuid "6c5b356e-1847-5521-9d23-2557c1554c47" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281610 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281610 1111 #uuid "2c24a4c5-5774-5e61-9500-ac29447b5de2" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281611 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281611 1111 #uuid "bda7d1bf-2be3-55d6-9338-f0cc39fd2b3a" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281612 1034 "I only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281612 1111 #uuid "86b056ee-6fd7-5a9b-90d6-a4641b906f0f" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281613 1034 "III only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281613 1111 #uuid "4dc1c01b-0fec-517d-99c1-76388bbf37c1" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281614 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281614 1111 #uuid "2b9df08e-5be5-561b-987c-e879133c9de7" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281616 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281617 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281618 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281619 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281620 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1041 "selection" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281620 13194139534193 true] [17592186281615 1110 #uuid "c597ab9b-1332-5810-9c9a-1684379ac297" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281616 1034 "h(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x-3}" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534193 true] [17592186281616 1111 #uuid "db442a7d-d3e2-529a-9d0a-6c69508a1724" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281617 1034 "f(x)=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{x-3}}" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534193 true] [17592186281617 1111 #uuid "efe17991-0589-557d-933d-2c09e635dbf5" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281618 1034 "g(x)=3|x-3|" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534193 true] [17592186281618 1111 #uuid "e5b1841a-1768-51da-a465-19b5a0c1181d" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281619 1034 "q(x)={\\begin{aligned}x-3, & x<3 \\\\ x+3, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534193 true] [17592186281619 1111 #uuid "9b585a37-6598-5862-aed2-90725e72015a" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281620 1034 "p(x)=\\sqrt{x}" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534193 true] [17592186281620 1111 #uuid "e398c7b3-8f1d-5e55-b5ce-3ab659a86fcf" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281622 13194139534193 true] [17592186281621 1089 "q-51067" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534193 true] [17592186281621 1100 "Given that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2$, has a cusp at $x=1,$ and is differentiable at $x=3$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\n- It is differentiable at $x=-2$\n- It's **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=f(3).$" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281621 1113 #uuid "b8948446-9f58-5a7d-8b94-5971514bef07" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281621 1145 "- Statement I is false. Continuity does not imply differentiability. For example, the function $y=|x+2|$ is continuous but it's not differentiable at $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a cusp at $x=1$, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is true. Differentiability implies continuity. Hence, ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=f(3).$" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281623 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281624 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281625 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281626 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281627 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1041 "selection" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281623 13194139534193 true] [17592186281622 1110 #uuid "d6654a34-2ccb-5cb7-a904-8088f96525ba" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281623 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534193 true] [17592186281623 1111 #uuid "1b337561-3369-5032-a520-339b3b5258f8" 13194139534193 true] [17592186281624 1034 "I and III only" 13